78: ## Offline SIF preparation
80: Word weights are a/(a+p(w)), with a=0.001. Frequencies match fse 1.x `lang_freq='en'`: English wordfreq best-list frequencies, converted to integer counts over 2**31-1 with a 1e-8 default, then normalized in float32.
82: - wordfreq version: 3.1.1
83: - component corpus: `HuggingFaceFW/fineweb-edu-llama3-annotations` at `72df4c92fb1b48beceb16016e8f695ec40a6c3a5`
84: - training paragraphs: 859346; seed: 0
85: - tokenized corpus checksum: `xxh3-128:88146a7f61a2c157c4710cfaf3e0cb4b`
86: - fitted weights and components checksum: `xxh3-128:7b81d9963c76f04d3d6be942b20ad3a9`
88: Ten uncentered components were fitted on that training corpus, never on the evaluation texts, then folded into the weighted table. Quantization follows folding. GloVe selected this corpus by the mean of STS-B Pearson, STS-B Spearman and NanoBEIR macro nDCG@10, each scaled to 0-100. Those benchmarks guided corpus selection, so their scores are not untouched holdout estimates. `preparation.json` records the full fit receipt.
90: Frequency-data attribution: [wordfreq](https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq) by Robyn Speer. Its code is Apache-2.0; its frequency data includes CC BY-SA 4.0 material and source-specific credits in [NOTICE.md](https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq/blob/master/NOTICE.md). Preparation transforms these frequencies into weights and folds them into the table. The source-vector license field does not waive those data terms.
